# Design technology workspace

This repository was initialized by the design technology foundation. The
foundation generated its starting files; from here on this README belongs to
you. Edit it freely.

## Ownership at a glance

| Location | Owner | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `firm/` | you | Identity, tokens, logos, fonts. The only input to generation. |
| Files listed in `.formwork/manifest.json` as `managed` | generator | Regenerated on every render. Edits are reported as conflicts and block the render until resolved. |
| Files listed as `seed` (this README, `docs/toolbar/toolbar_spec.md`, `.gitattributes`) | you | Written once if absent, never overwritten. |
| Everything else (your own tools, panels, docs) | you | Never touched by the generator. |

## Regenerate after changing `firm/`

From a foundation checkout:

```powershell
py -3.11 -m formwork_cli render --workspace <path-to-this-workspace> --dry-run
py -3.11 -m formwork_cli render --workspace <path-to-this-workspace>
```

The dry run is read-only and lists every create, update, delete, and conflict.

## Add your own pyRevit tools

Create a new panel folder inside the generated tab (for example
`extensions/<Extension>.extension/<Tab>.tab/Studio.panel/`) and register each
tool in `docs/toolbar/toolbar_spec.md`. Do not edit the generated sample panel
or `docs/toolbar/spec.d/`; those are managed.
